{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-95689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${e}^{2x}={({e}^{x})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u={e}^{x}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{({e}^{x})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95689" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f90777ae5e8d99b6573bcdf3db5baeee1de815c73c5c4c763864ff65e0c7adf"} {"question" "q-95689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{2x}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{x}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{2x}+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+C"] ["math" "{e}^{x}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{2x}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95689" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡{e}^{x}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-16}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-16}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{4}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-16}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f90777ae5e8d99b6573bcdf3db5baeee1de815c73c5c4c763864ff65e0c7adf"} {"question" "q-95852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95852" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{3}{1-9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{1-9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1-(3x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{artanh}⁡3x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this result is subject to the condition $|3x|<1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f90777ae5e8d99b6573bcdf3db5baeee1de815c73c5c4c763864ff65e0c7adf"} {"question" "q-95861" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95861" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{artanh}⁡9x+C"] ["math" "9\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{artanh}⁡3x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{artanh}⁡9x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95861" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{artanh}⁡3x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{2}{1-9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{2}{1-9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{1}{1-(3x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{1}{1-9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/12}\\frac{1}{1-(3x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{1-{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/4}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f90777ae5e8d99b6573bcdf3db5baeee1de815c73c5c4c763864ff65e0c7adf"} {"question" "q-95883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{3})"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-95883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-346522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+9}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-346522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+9}}\\,\\text{d}x=4{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse hyperbolic sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+9}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =12{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}} \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2-12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡0 \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2 \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-346522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f90777ae5e8d99b6573bcdf3db5baeee1de815c73c5c4c763864ff65e0c7adf"} {"question" "q-346522" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"} {"question" "q-346522" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12\\ln(2+\\sqrt{5})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070023/state.json" "file_sha256" "4645fff56b4977d74832f5a7852d4df48afa065dbfe3242843dc3f96bccd8157"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2439 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
